==========================================
  CROSS-NODE DLM RUN (rd vms-94c) -- every value below was read
  back out of the node's own executive, except the two WIRE counts,
  which come from the nodes' own passive captures:
    A: peer-mastered=OVMXA$X00 master_csid=0x00010002 releases_sent=0 blkasts_sent=1 unparsed=1 projections=agree
    B: peer-mastered=OVMXB$X01 master_csid=0x00010001 releases_sent=0 blkasts_sent=1 unparsed=1 projections=agree
    WIRE: op-0x03 deq frames=0  op-0x04 blkast frames=2

  FAILED (3a): an op-0x03 $DEQ was not emitted by both arms
  (A=0 B=0).

  AND THE ARM NEVER GOT AS FAR AS REFUSING: releases_no_wire_op
  is 0 on both, so the $DEQ never reached the requester FSM at
  all -- it died one step earlier, at posts_lock_gone
  (A=2 B=2). The engine posts a release to the FORK
  thread carrying only the lock id, and the fork thread REBUILDS
  the request from the lock database (vms_dlm_scs.c
  dlm_arm_run_post -> vms_lock_dlm_proxy_refill_post). For a
  $DEQ that rebuild can never succeed: the operation being
  transmitted is the one that destroys the proxy LKB it would be
  rebuilt from, and vms_deq_core tears that LKB down as soon as
  the post is queued. This is a PRODUCT GAP the rig measured,
  not a rig failure, and it is reported rather than worked
  around.
  FAILED (3a-wire): no op-0x03 frame appears in either node's
  capture. The executive counter and the wire agree that none
  crossed.
  FAILED (4): a node did not record receiving BOTH of the
  peer's cross-node frames (A unparsed=1 B unparsed=1;
  one op-0x03 + one op-0x04 each). Without the receive, the
  survival below proves nothing about them.
  --- what this run established ---
  HELD        both nodes MEMBER, CN=2, projections agree AFTER the phase
  HELD        a lock genuinely CROSSED: each node holds EX on a name its PEER masters
  HELD        op-0x04 BLKAST emitted by both arms AND seen on the wire
  NOT PROVEN  op-0x03 $DEQ emitted by both arms AND seen on the wire
  HELD        NEVER CRASH A PEER: each node RECEIVED a frame it has no receive half
              for, DECLINED it (counted), and stayed a sane member

